                  <msItem>
                     <title>Rad. Flaviacensis in Leviticum (2 fols.)</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Winchester Coll. 60A is a detached fragment of
                        All Souls Coll. 13; cf. N. R. Ker, Pastedown in Oxford bindings, pp. xi,
                        109.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Two leaves used as pastedowns in Ouvres de I.
                        Sleidan (Geneve, 1574), in contempoary Oxford binding (Gibson rolls xii,
                        xviii). They have been detached from the end of All Souls MS. 13. 16 more
                        leaves similarly used by the same binder are at All Souls in the bindings of
                        p.1.1--8.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">All Souls MS. 13 was given by the first warden,
                        Richard Andrew.</note>
                  </msItem>
